### How can you override the common pool's parallelism?

Use the system property: `-Djava.util.concurrent.ForkJoinPool.common.parallelism=16`. This affects the entire JVM. Prefer dedicated pools over changing the global setting.

### What are common mistakes?

```java
// WRONG: blocking IO on commonPool
CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> httpCall()); // blocks commonPool thread!

// WRONG: unbounded queue with no rejection policy
new ThreadPoolExecutor(10, 10, 0, SECONDS, new LinkedBlockingQueue<>());
// Queue grows without limit, OOM risk!

// CORRECT: dedicated pool with bounds and policy
CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> httpCall(), ioPool); // dedicated pool!
```

### What are common interview follow-up questions?

- Can you change commonPool at runtime? No, only via system properties at JVM start.
- What is CallerRunsPolicy? When the queue is full, the submitting thread runs the task itself, providing natural back-pressure.
- Does parallelStream use the same pool? Yes, parallelStream uses commonPool by default.
